Other APIs cover most use cases, but using TargetBasedAnimation directly lets you control the animation's play time. In the following example, you manually control the TargetBasedAnimation's play time based on the frame time provided by withFrameNanos.

val anim = remember {
    TargetBasedAnimation(
        animationSpec = tween(200),
        typeConverter = Float.VectorConverter,
        initialValue = 200f,
        targetValue = 1000f
    )
}
var playTime by remember { mutableLongStateOf(0L) }

LaunchedEffect(anim) {
    val startTime = withFrameNanos { it }

    do {
        playTime = withFrameNanos { it } - startTime
        val animationValue = anim.getValueFromNanos(playTime)
    } while (someCustomCondition())
}AnimationSnippets.kt

